From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:51:26 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: latch DCN 2.0 stereo flips at the stereo
 sync

A stereo surface (PLN_ADDR_TYPE_GRPH_STEREO) gives the HUBP a left-eye
address in DCSURF_PRIMARY_SURFACE_ADDRESS and a right-eye address in
DCSURF_SECONDARY_SURFACE_ADDRESS, and the OTG's stereo sync selects one
of them per frame. Every HUBP generation but DCN 2.0 also tells the HUBP
to take a new pair of addresses only at the stereo sync:
hubp1_program_surface_flip_and_addr() (DCN 1.0, 2.01) and
hubp21_program_surface_flip_and_addr() (DCN 2.1) set
SURFACE_FLIP_MODE_FOR_STEREOSYNC and SURFACE_FLIP_IN_STEREOSYNC for a
stereo surface and clear them otherwise; hubp3, hubp401, hubp42 and
hubp50 set SURFACE_FLIP_IN_STEREOSYNC.
hubp2_program_surface_flip_and_addr() programs the addresses but neither
field, although both are in the DCN 2.0 register list
(HUBP_MASK_SH_LIST_DCN_SHARE_COMMON), so a flip could land between the
two eyes of a pair, the left eye from one frame and the right eye from
the next.

Program them as DCN 2.1, its nearest relative, does: both set for a
stereo surface, both cleared when the surface stops being stereo. They
are written only when the new or the previous address is stereo, so 2D
flips program the same registers as before.

No caller builds a stereo address on DCN 2.0 today; amdgpu_dm does once
it sends frame-sequential stereo on DisplayPort. Not run on DCN 2.0
hardware (Navi 1x): the meaning of SURFACE_FLIP_MODE_FOR_STEREOSYNC is
taken from the DCN 1.0 and 2.1 code, not from a register reference.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/hubp/dcn20/dcn20_hubp.c  | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/hubp/dcn20/dcn20_hubp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/hubp/dcn20/dcn20_hubp.c
index cf2c9f800..012448d02 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/hubp/dcn20/dcn20_hubp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/hubp/dcn20/dcn20_hubp.c
@@ -742,6 +742,19 @@ bool hubp2_program_surface_flip_and_addr(
 	REG_UPDATE(VMID_SETTINGS_0,
 			VMID, address->vmid);
 
+	/*
+	 * A stereo surface flips at the stereo sync, so both eyes of a pair
+	 * come from the same surface, as DCN 1.0 and 2.1 program it. Written
+	 * only when stereo starts or ends, so 2D flips stay as they were.
+	 */
+	if (address->type == PLN_ADDR_TYPE_GRPH_STEREO ||
+	    hubp->request_address.type == PLN_ADDR_TYPE_GRPH_STEREO) {
+		bool stereo = address->type == PLN_ADDR_TYPE_GRPH_STEREO;
+
+		REG_UPDATE_2(DCSURF_FLIP_CONTROL,
+				SURFACE_FLIP_MODE_FOR_STEREOSYNC, stereo,
+				SURFACE_FLIP_IN_STEREOSYNC, stereo);
+	}
 
 	/* HW automatically latch rest of address register on write to
 	 * DCSURF_PRIMARY_SURFACE_ADDRESS if SURFACE_UPDATE_LOCK is not used
-- 
